Z||000000||2FAST4U||12-19-1999||03:02 AM||||All of my Fiero experience is with 4cyl cars and I just bought my first 6cyl today an 85 GT, so I have many questions.<P>1. The dog bone is shot and will need to be replaced but I noticed that the mounting brackets are out of alignment by about an inch. Is this normal or is there a problem.<P>2. In the engine compartment there is some kind of actuator mounted to the trunk bulkhead near the strut tower. It looks like an oversized EGR valve and it has a bracket on it where a cable used to be. What ever it is the engine seems to run OK with out it. I cant find any reference to it in any of my repair manuals. What is it?<P>The engine has a Holley throttle body. Is this OEM or aftermarket?<P>Does anyone make headers for this engine?<P>Thanks in advance. I'm sure I'll have more questions as soon as I geet it tagged so I can drive it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||03:23 AM||||I don't know much about V6s either as I can't pick my '85 GT up until next month <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">, but I do know that the Fiero Store sells headers.  The ones I see in the catalog are called, "Sprint V6 Performance manifold Set" and cost $549US.  Wow!  I hope they improve the performance considerably for that price!  Let me know how you like your '85 GT and if there are any other problems that I might want to know about.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||12-19-1999||10:00 AM||||I am also new to the v6 fiero, but I do know that the Holley throttle body is stock and you may have other engine/trans. mounts that are in need of repair if the dogbone is out of alignment. Also, get a polyurethan rebushing kit for the dogbone. I put a new GM dogbone on my 4 cyl car and it already needs replacing after less than 10 months.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||12-19-1999||11:03 AM||||If you're talking about a big vacuum operated valve thingie mounted close to the trunk and on the driver's side, that's probably the old cruise control servo. Does it have cruise control on the turn signal stalk, but maybe the CC doesn't work?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-19-1999||11:03 AM||||assuming you are talking about the left side of the trunk wall. it's the cruise unit. your car had cruise control and it's been hacked.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cobra427||12-19-1999||08:20 PM||||Here is another site that sells headers:http://home earthlink.net/~chriswest FOCOA does or did sell headers but who knows whats going on with them any more. Their catalog portion of their web site is still under construction||||reg||1
Z||000006||VR6boy||12-19-1999||08:55 PM||||I'll try here to redeem myself for my previous posts!(jeez sorry guys). 1-the dogbone SHOULD be in line, if the bushings are totally shot it could get out of line, the fiero store sells a very nice one w/ red poly bushings that will last forever for $40, if you don't fix this you'll ruin your tranny!. 2-thats your Cruise Control, 3- Holley made the stock throttle body, 4- i'm sure the fiero store can sell you good headers...One thing, stay away from Fiero Conversions in Canada -- they sold me a cat-back that was supposedly "stainless steel" that totally rusted out after a year! Not only did they charge me $300 for this piece of work, but tried to stick me with $100 customs/shipping charge!Gee thanks for nothing! -- Hopefully nobody here is affiliated with them, but in case there is, i want my $300 back!||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackGT||12-19-1999||11:35 PM||||2FAST4U<BR>I`ve just had a new rebuilt 2.8l put in my 86GT and before I did that I had my stock<BR>headers reinforced welded then I ground out<BR>the restrictions inside....WOW this made a <BR>world of difference! I`ve driven a GT like mine with those Sprint headers and I couldn`t<BR>tell the difference in power...although there<BR>was a slight difference in the tone. I think<BR>the $500 could be better spent elsewhere. Dude replace that dogbone with the one from the Fiero store! I also bought the performance suspension kit which I haven`t had an opportunity to put in but that same car I drove had all the bushings replaced with poly bushings and the ride was very firm<BR>but since I use my car as a daily driver I won`t be switching to poly bushings at all!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||dogtired||12-20-1999||03:36 AM||||Currently have 2 V6's daily drivers. One mine one my daughters. You have gotten a lot of great responses. Just wanted to mention, I had read a report somewhere, on how good the exhaust system is from the factory with just a little tweeking. Such as support welding the flanges (Ed Parks Fiero Factory, does great work) then clean them out, GM left a lot of junk in them. If you live in a place you can get away without a cat, that is in my opinion about the best you can do for a stock 2.8. exhaust.<BR>Now for the dogbone, If it is mismatched/out of line by an inch you had better check all your other motor tranny mounts. I would suppect one or more of the others are bad to make it off that far?<BR>These opinions are only mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just food for thought. You ask & I puke em up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>I didn't mean that, Lets just have fun and share  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||Carrolles||12-20-1999||09:50 AM||||I have an 85SE v-6 4spd.  I just replaced the engine and clutch.  While I had it apart I checked all the engine/trans mounts.  All were fine even with the misalignment  in the dogbone strut.  Mosalignment doesn't necessarily mean your other mounts are shot, but it's worth checking out anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||12-20-1999||07:03 PM||||near as I can tell, ignoring manufacturing error, only 2 things will make the strut, dogbone, brakets not line up nearly percet every time.<P>1. the engine mounts are bad or out os position. Holes for mounts are often slotted on either the frame or the engine side of the mounts.<P>2. the cradle bushings are bad. This lets the whole rear of the car move out of position.<P>there is a problem with having the bone crooked in that it pushed the motor toward the direction of the missalignment. Example, if the engine end is to the right of the trunk end the motor will push toward the right. Since it also twists when it does this, if our example was a 4 cyl it would want to push the alterantor pully into the strut tower.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-20-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroshop||12-20-1999||09:00 PM||||I am in the process of testing an all stainless steel header and we are looking to gain at least 20 HP. I will know more after  install the first unit on my 88GT and have it dynoed.<P>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 12-20-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 12-21-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||2FAST4U||12-21-1999||02:37 AM||||Bought all new motor mounts today and will order new urethane ddog bone and cradle mounts tomarrow. I figure since the car is pretty trashed as bought and I want to restore it to great conditiion I may as well replace them all at one time while I'm under the car.<P>Thanks<P>Joe||||reg||1
